    },
    "finalSym": "105",
    "answerSym": "48 + 57"
   },
   {
    "question": "In triangle $PQR$, the side $QR$ is extended to a point $S$ beyond $R$.\n$\\angle PRS = (4x + 10)^\\circ$, $\\angle QPR = (x + 20)^\\circ$ and $\\angle PQR = (2x + 15)^\\circ$.\nFind the value of $x$.",
    "level": "ordinary",
    "marks": 10,
    "workedSolution": {
     "steps": [
      {
       "title": "Use Theorem 6",
       "lines": [
        {
         "text": "$\\angle PRS$ is the exterior angle at $R$. It equals the sum of the opposite interior angles $\\angle QPR$ and $\\angle PQR$."
        },
        {
         "tex": "4x + 10 &= (x + 20) + (2x + 15)",
         "sym": "Eq(4*x + 10, (x + 20) + (2*x + 15))",
         "new": true
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "title": "Simplify",
       "lines": [
        {
         "tex": "4x + 10 &= 3x + 35",
         "sym": "Eq(4*x + 10, 3*x + 35)"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "title": "Solve for $x$",
       "lines": [
        {
         "tex": "x &= 35 - 10",
         "sym": "Eq(x, 35 - 10)",
         "new": true
        },
        {
         "tex": "&= 25",
         "sym": "Eq(x, 25)"
        }
       ]
      }
     ],
     "finalAnswer": "x = 25"
    },
    "finalSym": "[25]",
    "answerSym": "solve(Eq(4*x + 10, (x + 20) + (2*x + 15)), x)"
   },
